  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.9.12 — Viewer now recovers when the host restarts its stream while the channel stays up (e.g. a new SessionHost numbering frames from 1 on a desktop switch): a large backward video-sequence jump rebases and repaints instead of dropping every frame as stale. Tunable via ViewerOptions.StreamRestartSeqDrop (default 256). Additive, no API breaks.\n0.9.11 — License authority moved to the central AccountManagement service (embedded central public key; the signed payload `product` must be `sessionkit`). The package is now a plain Release build (no obfuscation) — public API unchanged, more reliable and easier to debug.\n0.9.10 — Expose the H264Nal Annex-B helper (public) with an allocation-free IsKeyframe, so an integrator forwarding raw H.264 to a browser (WebCodecs) can label keyframes without re-implementing NAL scanning. Additive, no API breaks.\n\n0.9.9 — Since 0.9.0, all verified on real Windows/Linux/macOS hardware: 3-OS audio plus two-way audio (operator mic → host), an audio jitter buffer, cursor overlay (incl. macOS NSCursor), adaptive quality with dynamic H.264 bitrate, sequence-numbered loss recovery, auto-reconnect, multi-monitor (enumerate + switch), macOS clipboard, viewer→host file upload, and a session control-approval consent gate.\n\nThis release also introduces the Standard (free) / Premium (licensed) split: Premium features unlock at runtime via SessionKitLicense.Activate(key) and degrade gracefully (or throw when explicitly constructed) without one. A Suite bundle key (SessionKit Premium + ServerKit) unlocks Premium too.\n\nPart of the RemoteViewer family — Connection = ConnectKit (free), Session = SessionKit, Server = ServerKit. Downloads, 5-minute quickstarts, and Premium/Suite keys: https://www.remote-viewer.com/downloads",
